# Objects: making them, carrying them, wearing them, putting them in things,
# and the refusals. Played by the implementor, because `load` is the only way
# to get an object into an empty world without walking to a shop.
Parityone
y
swordfish
swordfish
m
w

1
goto 3001
load obj 3021
inventory
wield sword
equipment
remove sword
load obj 3032
put sword bag
look in bag
get sword bag
load obj 3041
wear shirt
load obj 3042
wear shield
equipment
remove all
inventory
drop sword
look
get sword
# The same word, with a count in front of it: `isname` is a whole-word match
# and `get_number` is what reads the "2." (5m).
load obj 3021
get 2.sword
inventory
junk all
inventory
# Looking at things, which is four different functions behind one word:
# look_in_obj for `in`, look_in_direction for a direction, look_at_target for
# everything else, and look_at_room for nothing at all (act.informative.c:679).
# The extra-description search is what makes `look at atm` show the note stuck
# to the machine rather than the machine's own line from the room.
load obj 3021
look at sword
look sword
drop sword
look sword
look at atm
look north
look d
look 0.sword
look .sword
get sword
# Refusals, whose wording matters exactly as much as the successes.
get nothing
wear nothing
wield nothing
remove nothing
put nothing in nothing
drop nothing
look in nothing
quit
